The product
-----------

The product binary is `zypi` (Cargo package `pi-pager-bin`). It is a terminal
UI. It starts the Python agent (`python -m pi_agent_cli`) and talks to it over
standard ACP on stdio. Override the command with `PI_AGENT_COMMAND` or
`PI_PYTHON`. The home directory is `PI_HOME` (`GROK_HOME` is still read when
`PI_HOME` is not set), or `~/.pi-python`.

Modifications relative to upstream
----------------------------------

Every change is in the pi-python git history under tui/. This list is a
summary of the changes (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)). The plan
docs/PLAN/PLAN-RUST-AGENT-RUNTIME-REMOVAL.md and its execution log give the
details of each removal.

- At vendor time: moved the Cargo workspace from the root of the grok-build
  repository into tui/ of the pi-python monorepo. Added this NOTICE and
  .gitattributes (LF for shebangs and Rust sources, so that Windows checkouts
  do not break bin/protoc). Removed the PTY e2e crates (`ptyctl`,
  `ptyctl-cli`, `pi-grok-pager-pty-harness`).
- Replaced the in-process Rust agent runtime with the Python agent. Removed
  the `pi-sampler` crate and the runtime parts of `pi-shell` (model sampling,
  the agent loop, the leader process, headless mode). The pager now only
  speaks standard ACP to the agent.
- Removed the screens, commands and crates that need that runtime (for
  example: the agents, subagents, tasks, workflows, goals and MCP screens,
  hooks and plugins, rewind and fork, the dashboard). The slash commands are
  limited to a short fixed list.
- Renamed the crates from `xai-grok-*` to `pi-*` (for example, the product
  crate is now `pi-pager-bin`). Renamed the product to `zypi`. Changed the
  names that a user sees (themes, notifications, paths, help text).
- Reduced the embedded user guide to the pages that describe `zypi`. `zypi`
  no longer writes the guide to disk at start.
- Added tests and tools for the ACP link between the pager and the Python
  agent (see scripts/tui_baseline.py, scripts/tui_pty/ and
  crates/codegen/pi-pager/tests/python_agent_e2e.rs).

